    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nA detached four-bedroom bungalow in a superb seaside village location brought to market by DNG Duffy\n\nA rare opportunity to acquire a detached four-bedroom bungalow just minutes from the sea in the heart of Blackrock village.\n\nNo. 33 Beech Park offers an exciting opportunity to create a wonderful family home in one of County Louth's most sought-after coastal locations. Extending to approximately 106.9 sq. m. (1,151 sq. ft.), this detached bungalow offers generous single-storey accommodation, four bedrooms and excellent potential for modernisation and personalisation.\n\nThe property is a genuine blank canvas, allowing the successful purchaser the opportunity to transform and modernise the existing accommodation to their own taste and requirements or is home ready as it is.\n\nThe accommodation comprises an entrance hall, living room, separate dining room off kitchen, four bedrooms and two bathrooms. The property is heated by oil-fired central heating.\nThe living room is a particularly bright space, with generous glazing bringing plenty of natural light into the room. The dining room provides excellent additional living space and could potentially offer flexibility for a future purchaser wishing to reconfigure the accommodation, subject to the necessary permissions.\n\nThe four bedrooms provide excellent flexibility for family living, guest accommodation, home office use or simply having the additional space that is increasingly sought after in today's homes. The two bathrooms are another practical benefit of the layout.\n\nThe location is exceptional.\nOne of the property's greatest attractions is its position within easy walking distance of Blackrock's seafront and promenade. The beach and coast are close enough to become part of everyday life — ideal for morning walks, evening strolls or simply enjoying the fresh sea air.\nThe village itself offers a wonderful selection of local amenities, including cafés, shops, Centra, restaurants and everyday services, all within a short walk of the property.\nFamilies will particularly appreciate the proximity of local schools, while Blackrock Park offers an excellent recreational space close to home.\nBlackrock combines the charm of a traditional seaside village with excellent everyday convenience, making it an increasingly desirable place to live. The ability to walk to the sea, school, park, cafés and village amenities is a genuine lifestyle advantage.\n\n\nDisclaimer:\nThese particulars do not form part of any offer or contract. All statements are provided for informational purposes only and should not be relied upon as representations of fact. Intending purchasers must independently verify the accuracy of each statement through inspection or other means. Configurations of kitchens, bathrooms, wardrobes, and other features may be subject to change without prior notice. Purchasers are advised to confirm the current specification at the time of booking. Neither the Vendor, Selling Agent, nor any of their employees or representatives have the authority to make or give any representation or warranty in relation to any property. Images and artist's impressions are for illustrative purposes only. Floor plans are not to scale, and all dimensions are approximate."
      },
